  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project Preparation Assistance Facility</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project Preparation Assistance Facility (PPAF) will help Cambodia improve project readiness by financing detailed engineering designs and bidding documents for priority infrastructure projects across sectors such as transport, energy, health, agriculture, water, digital, and tourism. The facility supports the government&amp;apos;s Public Investment Management System Reform Strategy and Project Development Facility to ensure technically sound, implementation-ready projects, reduce startup delays, and enhance quality-at-entry. With an estimated cost of $15.43 million (ADB concessional loan: $15.0 million), PPAF will engage consultants for design and procurement preparation, accelerating the transition from concept to execution and enabling efficient, high-quality project implementation during its 2026-2032 implementation period.</narrative>
  </description>
